y_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20048, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EB744ZQtdYEtYdqPEjgx9t", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20048, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WTbxZykuDLnLsxBymaKpJ4", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 20348, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WTbxZykuDLnLsxBymaKpJ4", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20348, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WTbxZykuDLnLsxBymaKpJ4", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25447, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_018X2sHAWufUiHEPprmwmSBf", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway through: the orchestrator stopped after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A second attempt finished in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west; service healthy; error rate about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56047, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_018X2sHAWufUiHEPprmwmSBf", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56047, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_018X2sHAWufUiHEPprmwmSBf", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58022, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01NPjieu9VWQJ8h3QqSArC1R", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58322, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01NPjieu9VWQJ8h3QqSArC1R", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58322, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01NPjieu9VWQJ8h3QqSArC1R", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63670, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Status before the rollback:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The test version before it (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n2. **Target version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. It had already been healthy there before, so the change-manager approval rule didn't apply.\n3. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of a system error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Re-running the same rollback was safe, so I tried again and it finished in all regions. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n4. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. The incident had been created (INC-0001, which paged on-call), so I didn't send it a second time and there's no duplicate page. Its description covers the failure, the partial first rollback, the current state, and two follow-ups: why v2.3.1 failed, and what caused the error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BHBibw7dqdndgcFmoDW6Af", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TEmiuG2iKudQGDjjRwonb8", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QZbAFmy4cHYfVTpimcFK6L", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_0145zHMR2yL3f1fw6wB41T1u", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback only finished in us-east. Rolling back to the same target version is safe to repeat, so I'll try once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015qeFZjpjyfNg2gL4gssa9U", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01EB744ZQtdYEtYdqPEjgx9t", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01WTbxZykuDLnLsxBymaKpJ4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_018X2sHAWufUiHEPprmwmSBf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After checkout-api v2.3.1 was deployed, it failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc had also been unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt failed partway through: the orchestrator stopped after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A second attempt finished in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west; service healthy; error rate about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NPjieu9VWQJ8h3QqSArC1R", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as INC-0001.\n\n1. **Status before the rollback:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It was failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The test version before it (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy in staging.\n2. **Target version:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. It had already been healthy there before, so the change-manager approval rule didn't apply.\n3. **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of a system error, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. Re-running the same rollback was safe, so I tried again and it finished in all regions. All three regions are now on v2.3.0, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n4. **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. The incident had been created (INC-0001, which paged on-call), so I didn't send it a second time and there's no duplicate page. Its description covers the failure, the partial first rollback, the current state, and two follow-ups: why v2.3.1 failed, and what caused the error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}